2026-08-18T15:10:27.6375829Z > # in docs/dev-log/release/0.7.0-cran-gate/test-timings.csv): the CRAN lane ran
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6376558Z > # 1160 s locally and 29-30 min of `checking tests` on win-builder, far above
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6377480Z > # CRAN's ~10-minute incoming guidance. Seventeen files carried 747 s of that
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6378227Z > # 1160 s; excluding them leaves 413 s locally (~6.9 min), projecting to ~10 min
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6378918Z > # on Windows at the measured 1.50x local->win-builder factor.
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6379403Z > #
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6379885Z > # These are statistical-validation suites -- bivariate association sandwiches,
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6380700Z > # the G4/G5 missing-response foundation, zero-one-beta, bivariate Gaussian, and
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6381535Z > # the profile-target matrix -- not "does the package install and work" tests.
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6382304Z > # They still run in full in repository CI, where NOT_CRAN=true. Nothing is
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6383034Z > # deleted and no test is weakened; this only changes which lane runs them.
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6383588Z > #
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6384045Z > # The patterns are ANCHORED on purpose. An unanchored "zero-one-beta" also
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6384820Z > # matches test-missing-predictor-zero-one-beta.R, and an unanchored
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6385909Z > # "biv-gaussian" also matches test-missing-response-biv-gaussian.R -- neither is
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6386626Z > # intended, and both must keep running on the CRAN lane.
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6387111Z > #
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6387589Z > # `^julia` excludes every test-julia-*.R file. That alone is NOT enough: CRAN-lane
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6388378Z > # files such as test-binomial-response.R still call engine = "julia" inside
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6389160Z > # expect_error(), and Workflow G now admits fixed-effect binomial into the Julia
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6389993Z > # bridge, so the call reaches JuliaCall::julia_setup() before any rejection.
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6390755Z > # Ligges win-builder (2026-08-16/17) hung there for ~10448s even after #1061.
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6391506Z > # Defense in depth: (1) this filter, (2) drm_skip_live_julia() in live tests,
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6392518Z > # (3) drm_julia_setup() hard-blocks the CRAN lane unless DRMTMB_JULIA_TESTS=true.
2026-08-18T15:10:27.6393172Z > # The full suite still runs when NOT_CRAN=true.
