2026-08-18T15:10:28.0839591Z > ### Name: random_effect_scale_formulas
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0839719Z > ### Title: Random-effect scale formula syntax
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0839905Z > ### Aliases: random_effect_scale_formulas sd sd1 sd2 sd_phylo sd_phylo1
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0839998Z > ###   sd_phylo2
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0840088Z > 
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0840173Z > ### ** Examples
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0840256Z > 
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0840376Z > bf(y ~ x + (1 | id), sigma ~ z, sd(id) ~ habitat)
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0840469Z <drm_formula>
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0840555Z y ~ x + (1 | id)
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0840646Z sigma ~ z
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0840738Z sd(id) ~ habitat
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0840821Z > 
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0840908Z > bf(
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0841006Z +   mu1 = y1 ~ x + (1 | p | id),
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0841103Z +   mu2 = y2 ~ x + (1 | p | id),
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0841195Z +   sd1(id) ~ habitat,
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0841283Z +   sd2(id) ~ habitat,
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0841374Z +   rho12 = ~ x
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0841455Z + )
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0841726Z <drm_formula>
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0841824Z mu1 = y1 ~ x + (1 | p | id)
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0841920Z mu2 = y2 ~ x + (1 | p | id)
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0842014Z sd1(id) ~ habitat
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0842100Z sd2(id) ~ habitat
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0842190Z rho12 = ~x
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0842276Z > 
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0842363Z > bf(
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0842486Z +   y ~ x + phylo(1 | species, tree = tree),
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0842619Z +   sd(species, level = "phylogenetic") ~ ecology
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0842708Z + )
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0842795Z <drm_formula>
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0842905Z y ~ x + phylo(1 | species, tree = tree)
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0843026Z sd(species, level = "phylogenetic") ~ ecology
2026-08-18T15:10:28.0843112Z > 
